    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5523" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bōla</span></b> , ae (in <i><span class="en">Liv. 4, 49,
			6 sq.</span></i>
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bōlae</span></b> , ārum),
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βῶλα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a very ancient town of
				the Æqui</i>, <i>in Latium</i>, now <i>Poli</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 6, 775</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bōlānus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to Bola</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					4, 49, 11</span></i>
			.— And <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bōlāni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Bola</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 4, 49,
				3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 9, § 69</span></i>.</div>
